<title>CHINA: Shanghai newspaper to print on silk for HK handover.</title>
<headline>Shanghai newspaper to print on silk for HK handover.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shanghai's Wen Hui Daily, one of the city's major newspapers, will print a limited edition on silk to mark the return of Hong Kong to Chinese rule on July 1, the newspaper said in an advertisement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The newspaper will print 5,800 copies of a special July 1 commemorative edition on coloured silk and the issue will sell for 5,000 yuan ($600) each.</p>
<p>The silk souvenir would last for more than 500 years and comes with a certificate of authenticity, it said.</p>
<p>The British colony of Hong Kong reverts to Chinese sovereignty at midnight on June 30. Chinese stamp and coin dealers report brisk business in souvenirs marking the event.</p>
</text>
